# CLAUDE.local.md — private overlay

**Gitignored.** Project-private supplement to `CLAUDE.md`. Auto-loaded by Claude Code; never reaches the public repo. Workspace backup: `tick-trader-percore-workspace/CLAUDE.local.md.backup` via `/sync-workspace`.

**Purpose:** index of operator-specific overlay on top of CLAUDE.md baseline — required-reading triggers, sprint state pointer, going-forward rule index (each entry ≤3 lines; bodies live in canonical docs), auto-write contracts, skill load contracts, privacy boundary, landmines pointer.

**Each going-forward rule = one-line trigger + canonical-doc pointer.** Deep-dive bodies (Why + How to apply + worked examples + anti-patterns + specific event context) live in:

- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DESIGN_SPECS/<pattern>.md` — pattern bodies (HOW)
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DOCS/DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` — master settings portal (WHY + meta-rules; § 11.5 is the meta-discipline registry)
- `DOCS/RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS.md` — anti-pattern registry
- `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md`, `DOCS/PARITY_ISSUES.md`, `FEATURE_LOOKUP.md` — auto-write ledgers
- `~/.claude/projects/-home-caramel-code-FoxML-Trader-v2/memory/` — operator-collaboration + project + reference memories
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/claude-skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` — operational skill contracts
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/DOCS/LANDMINES.md` — operational pitfalls

## Meta-disciplines (audit-methodology gaps codified)

When SHAPE audits return GREEN/YELLOW after 3+ iterations but blind spots persist, the META gap itself is the signal. See `DOCS/DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` § 11.5 for the canonical meta-discipline registry. Currently codified: **M1** sister-registry parity verification / **M2** cross-tool emit-site enumeration / **M3** anti-pattern codification distinguishes legitimate siblings / **M4** implementation-detail audit layer above SHAPE (taxonomy at `DESIGN_SPECS/implementation-layer-blindspot-taxonomy.md`; skill at `/blindspot-scan`) / **M5** train-serve execution-layer parity (Stage 3 first canonical at `.B.4` ship close via EngineCommon extract) / **M6** body-content arg enumeration before helper extract (`feedback_enumerate_helper_signature_args_before_extract`; `/readiness` Check 33) / **M7** structural enforcement when memory codification proves insufficient (`structural-enforcement-when-memory-insufficient.md` Stage 3 first canonical via B-Plus CI tool + `/capture-audit` skill; sister memory `feedback_structural_enforcement_when_memory_insufficient`). Adding a new Mn → procedure in DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY § 11.5.

