## Going-forward rules (index)

Each rule = one-line trigger + canonical doc pointer. Body lives in
the canonical doc.

### Code & design

- **Structural fix preferred when bug class can recur** (2026-05-09) — `CLAUDE.md § Design philosophy` (Maintenance gradient); `DESIGN_SPECS/structural-fix-preferred-decision-framework.md`. Trigger: same pattern at multiple sites drifted apart → registry/helper-extract with compile-time enforcement.
- **Framework discipline over ad-hoc per-instance code when recurrence is foreseeable** (2026-05-14) — `CLAUDE.md § Design philosophy` (Maintenance gradient — framework-driven); `DESIGN_SPECS/pattern-codification-lifecycle.md`. Trigger: ≥2 future applications projected AND bug class can recur AND framework cost ≤ projected savings × N → invest upfront.
- **Boundary-stable refactors over wide cascades** (2026-05-06) — `feedback_reduce_touch_sites.md`. Trigger: refactor crosses ≥4 files → propose stable boundary first.
- **Cohort-audit when new cfg field has 2+ siblings** (2026-05-11) — `DESIGN_SPECS/cfg-flag-eligibility-criteria.md`. Trigger: new boolean cfg field with 2+ semantic siblings → audit cohort.
- **Categorical applicability for new cfg fields** (2026-05-14) — `DESIGN_SPECS/categorical-tag-applicability-pattern.md`. Trigger: new cfg field → fill applies_to_* columns; no hardcoded enum names in gating.
- **Cross-file cfg surfaces use `lives_in_struct`** (2026-05-14) — same doc § Cross-file. Trigger: cfg field in non-default cfg file → tag with `lives_in_struct` enum.
- **Bitmap overflow static_assert is mandatory** (2026-05-14) — `DESIGN_SPECS/bitmap-overflow-protection-discipline.md`. Trigger: any FOREACH_X-paired bitmap field → co-located `static_assert(COUNT <= sizeof(type)*8)`.
- **Type-trait dispatch via `tt::` namespace for typed registry dispatchers** (2026-05-14) — `CLAUDE.md H13` (invariant); `DESIGN_SPECS/type-trait-dispatch-via-tt-namespace.md`. Trigger: building registry-driven dispatcher → use `tt::<verb>_field<T>` with destination-by-reference + type-family static_assert. NEVER `*reinterpret_cast<X*>(...)` punning.
- **Multi-bit state encoding for K-state fields (K = 2..16)** (2026-05-13) — `DESIGN_SPECS/multi-bit-state-encoding-pattern.md`. Trigger: new K-state field → N-bit packed slot (N=ceil(log2 K)) + branchless inference API.
- **Cfg↔ML surface-alignment audit at every ML feature add** (2026-05-14) — RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS Class 24; `CLAUDE.md § Design philosophy` (Maintenance gradient). Trigger: new ML capability → answer 4 columns (cfg parse / Settings render / Stamp tag / Per-core override). Fire `/ml-audit` at sub-ship close.
- **Decision-time data binding for per-instance cfg values** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_SPECS/decision-time-data-binding-pattern.md`; Class 27. Trigger: subsystem needs cfg value at per-fill/event time → pre-resolve onto in-flight object at decision time. FORBIDDEN: scalar cfg-mirror field on subsystem state.
- **Registries optimize for ADDING; principle + sweep optimizes for ELIMINATING** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` § 1.5. Trigger: considering new registry → ask "should this pattern accumulate (registry good) OR shrink (registry counterproductive)?"
- **Branchless dispatch preferred for SP/HP data-dependent code** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_SPECS/branchless-dispatch-discipline.md`; Class 28. Trigger: data-dependent dispatch on SP/HP/drainer/producer code → fn pointer table / 2D state×type table / pre-resolve. Real-world mispredict is 30-100ns.
- **Audit hand-waves proactively when "branch is fine" framing surfaces** (2026-05-15) — same doc § "The hand-wave anti-pattern". Trigger: "branch is fine because predictor handles it" OR "mispredict is only 5-15ns" → STOP; re-examine through determinism + p99 lens.
- **Audit invocations specify scope per situation** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_SPECS/audit-scope-taxonomy.md`. Trigger: invoking audit skill → specify scope (current / wide / scoped <glob> / module:<name> / chain:<symbol>). Default `current`; reserve `wide` for quarterly + post-codification.
- **Multi-state dispatch with per-state metadata when N-state enum exhibits asymmetric behavior** (2026-05-16) — `DESIGN_SPECS/multi-state-dispatch-with-per-state-update-metadata.md`. Trigger: dispatch enum has ≥3 states + behavior splits along ≥2 orthogonal axes → encode in X-macro row metadata columns; auto-compute dispatch tables.
- **Audit canonical sister before proposing new framework infrastructure** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_audit_canonical_sister_before_new_infra.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/canonical-sister-extension-discipline.md`. Trigger: plan proposing new registry/bit/dispatch/sidecar/macro → grep codebase for canonical sister patterns FIRST; if ≥50% overlap + same consumer behavior → EXTEND.
- **Framework-layer payoff has diminishing returns; stop at the inflection point** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_framework_layer_payoff_diminishing_returns.md`. Trigger: tempted to propose new framework layer past inflection. Recognition: sites-added-vs-eliminated (60:4 ship; 6:5 reject); walker iterating zero rows; audit catches small-duplication territory. Lifecycle: build (ARCHITECT bias OK) → consolidation (aggressive framework) → post-inflection (this discipline) → maintenance (code-moving wins). Phase transitions operator-signaled.
- **Proportionate response to audit findings** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_proportionate_response_to_audit_findings.md`. Trigger: audit catches structural issue. Surface full menu (A INLINE MERGE / B ACCEPT WITH RATIONALE / C FOLD / D ARCHITECT + NO-FOLD first-of-kind) + evaluate each honestly + pick what's actually right (not first sufficient; not smallest). Audit catch is information; response is judgment.
- **Plan right, not fast** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_plan_right_not_fast.md`. Trigger: planning-grade decision. Planning IS the hard part of SWE in 2026; AI handles mechanical coding; human value-add concentrates in planning. Disciplines support decide-rightly, not decide-quickly. Indecisiveness is feature; speed heuristics undercut planning depth.
- **4-pillar self-audit before surfacing recommendations** — `feedback_audit_own_proposals_with_same_rigor.md`. Trigger: before surfacing ANY recommendation. 4 pillars: DESIGN_SPECS cross-check / anti-pattern catalog check / operator-impact / novel-alternative. `/readiness` Checks 31-33 verify. Sister memories: `feedback_recheck_designspecs_on_pushback`, `feedback_surface_operator_migration_path_proactively`, `feedback_proactive_novel_alternative_consideration`.
- **Future-headache vs optimization scope framework** — `feedback_future_headache_vs_optimization_scope_framework.md`. Trigger: scope discoveries during refactor/cleanup. Anti-pattern instance survival = close at ship; pure perf optimization = defer + document.
- **Iteration spiral as audit-meta-gap signal** — `feedback_iteration_spiral_signals_audit_meta_gap.md`. Trigger: plan body amendments find smaller-and-smaller findings across 4+ cycles. STOP individual-finding-chase; codify META-gap immediately per `DOCS/DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` § 11.5 procedure; verify inflection. Common meta-gap shapes: consumer enumeration / cross-pattern access / cross-file-type / sister-registry / naming-asymmetry.
- **Comprehensive consumer enumeration before registry-row deletion** — `feedback_enumerate_consumers_before_registry_row_deletion.md`. Trigger: plan proposes X-macro registry row deletion / rename / column-1-vs-source-name change. Run ONE comprehensive grep covering all access patterns across all file types BEFORE plan body lock. Sister: `feedback_audit_canonical_sister_before_new_infra` (producer side; this is consumer side).
- **Implementation-detail audit layer (M4) above SHAPE** — `feedback_implementation_detail_blindspot_recovery_via_taxonomy.md`. Trigger: SHAPE audits return GREEN/YELLOW after 3+ iterations OR struct-gen migration crosses ≥2 registries OR type unification OR cross-registry consumer OR macro hoisting OR wire-format ordering change. Fire `/blindspot-scan` against the 12-category taxonomy at `DESIGN_SPECS/implementation-layer-blindspot-taxonomy.md`.
- **Framework-driven CLI binary for cross-tool wire-format surfaces (≥3 recurrence)** (2026-05-18) — `DESIGN_SPECS/framework-driven-cli-binary-pattern.md`. Trigger: cross-tool surface (typically `tools/*.sh`) emits wire format that mirrors engine emit; Layer 7 § cross-tool emit-site enumeration catches recurring drift (≥3 sync events) → STRUCTURAL FIX preferred over discipline-application. Replace bash with thin C++ CLI binary calling engine framework API directly (no mirror; drift impossible by construction). Sister: `wire-format-byte-preservation-discipline.md` Layer 7 (the DISCIPLINE; this rule is the STRUCTURAL-FIX upgrade); `feedback_structural_fix_for_recurring_class.md` (parent meta-rule); `feedback_no_defer_for_effort.md` (the rule that catches "bash patches at this ship → C++ migration later ship" as effort-deferral when same surface). Skip when: cross-tool surface lacks framework-driven C++ equivalent OR operator workflow needs bash-only OR recurrence count < 3.
- **B-Plus CI tool — compile-time plan body symbol verification at COMMIT layer** (2026-05-26) — `tools/check_plan_body_symbol_existence.py` + pre-commit hook at `.git/hooks/pre-commit` + `/readiness` Check 32. Trigger: any plan body .md edit (auto-invoked at commit time). Extracts ```cpp blocks, derives includes, compiles via g++, classifies failures (FABRICATION vs HARNESS-ISSUE). Bypass with `SKIP_PLAN_BODY_CHECK=1` env (use sparingly). Sister checks: Check 33 (M6 body-content arg enumeration); Check 34 (tiered-audit declaration). Parent memory: `feedback_verify_symbol_existence_at_plan_drafting_time` (Stage 6 cadence-locked); `feedback_structural_fix_for_recurring_class` (parent: structural enforcement beats memory codification alone — 6 NEW Class 14 fabrications introduced in-cycle AFTER M6 codification proved insufficient at v5.15.5.F.4d.1.B.4 v1.7.3→v1.7.4). Extend `SYMBOL_INCLUDES` / `CALLER_SCOPE_PREFIXES` / `KNOWN_HARNESS_FN_MISMATCHES` maps as new symbols/patterns surface.
- **`/capture-audit` skill — mechanical decision-capture drift check** (2026-05-26) — runs as pre-commit gate (via `/sync-workspace`) + pre-handoff gate (via `/handoff`) + standalone. 10 checks: MEMORY.md sync / plan body frontmatter (`audit_tier:` + `sister_specs:`) / decision-log artifact existence / sentinel matching (`<!-- D/C/F: <id> -->` + `<!-- STATUS: <state> -->`) / handoff doc currency (PENDING items vs git log) / Stage 6 promotion candidates per M7 / DESIGN_SPECS Stage 2→3 promotion eligibility / skill-in-CLAUDE.md-suite linkage (recursive trust anchor) / memory→DESIGN_SPECS sister cross-ref / CLAUDE.local.md going-forward rules currency. Exit 0=clean / 1=findings; `--strict` blocks. Sister: M7 parent (`structural-enforcement-when-memory-insufficient.md`); session decision log discipline (`feedback_session_decision_log_discipline`).
- **Session decision log discipline** (2026-05-26) — `feedback_session_decision_log_discipline.md`; template at `claude-skills/capture-audit/decision-log-template.md`. Trigger: planning cycle > 3 amendments OR multi-session ship. Per-version sidecar at `plans/<sprint>/decision-logs/<plan-name>-v<version>.md`. Captures Decisions (operator-decided) + Commitments (claude-said-will-do) + Discoveries (new findings) + STATUS (pending/landed/dropped/deferred). Plan body uses `<!-- D/C/F: <id> -->` + `<!-- STATUS: <state> -->` sentinel markers. `/capture-audit` Check 3+4 enforce. Closes rabbit-hole-amnesia failure mode. Sister: feedback_structural_enforcement_when_memory_insufficient (M7 parent); feedback_iteration_spiral_signals_audit_meta_gap (recognition trigger).
- **`/accept-handoff` skill — receiver-side handoff verification** (2026-05-26) — fresh-session pickup runs ONE command to: read handoff doc + load all "Critical pickup-time reads" files + run `/capture-audit --deep` (verify NO drift since handoff written) + run `/readiness` against in-flight plan body + read CLAUDE.md/local.md/MEMORY.md baseline + recreate TaskList from handoff Stage 1.5 capture + verify engine + workspace git state matches handoff claims + output PICKUP-READY status + concrete next-action. Closes "fresh session forgets to load required reading" failure mode. Sister to `/handoff` (writer side); `/capture-audit` (drift check at receiver-time).

### Thread isolation between subsystems

- **GUI ↔ HP/SP thread isolation: NEVER share state directly** (2026-05-14) — `DESIGN_SPECS/universal-registry-bitmap-dispatcher-pattern.md` § GUI ↔ engine. Trigger: new subsystem touching engine state from different thread → typed mirror per side; communicate via file + reload-signal; NEVER pointer-share. Aligns with H3.

### Process & sprint

- **Suggest mid-sprint audits when work impacts downstream** (2026-05-10). Trigger: HIGH-RISK ship just shipped / first pattern application / cross-cutting changes → suggest `/test-strength-audit` + `/dod-audit` + `/parity-check`; wait for greenlight.
- **Sub-plan sidecar files for substantial sections with implementation code samples** (2026-05-16) — convention: `<plan-name>-examples.md`. Trigger: section spans multi-file coordination OR architectural decision points OR >100 LOC OR new framework pattern → create sidecar.
- **Each DESIGN_SPECS doc has a CLAUDE.md cross-ref** (2026-05-09). Format: `Pattern documented in DESIGN_SPECS/<name>.md.` at end of relevant CLAUDE.md item.
- **Codify design principles in CLAUDE.md as patterns mature** (2026-05-09). Promote to CLAUDE.md once: ≥2 codebase applications OR DESIGN_SPECS doc exists, AND pattern is broad.
- **Auto-pick the more future-oriented design option when trade-off is clear** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_auto_pick_future_oriented.md`. Surface ONLY when (a) future-vs-now trade-off genuinely sharp OR (b) I genuinely don't know which is more future-oriented. Never punt with "your call" framing on auto-decidable decisions.
- **Audit → update → implement → ship cycle PER sub-ship** (2026-05-17). Trigger: each sub-ship in multi-sub-ship umbrella → `/precoding-audit-gate` → triage + consult → update plan → implement → ship + postmortem. Bank rest as TECH_DEBT.
- **Plans introducing new registries cite existing sister registry inspection** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_plans_cite_sister_registry_inspection.md`; `/readiness` Check 29. Trigger: plan proposes new registry/bit/dispatch/sidecar/macro → MUST include "Canonical sister registries considered" header section with per-candidate verdict.
- **Anti-spaghetti audit on cadence** (2026-05-17) — `project_anti_spaghetti_audit_cadence.md`. Trigger: quarterly codebase-wide run + post-new-anti-pattern-codification sweep + ad-hoc.
- **New plans use future-oriented plan template** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_new_plans_use_future_oriented_template.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/future-oriented-plan-template.md`. Required sections: Design space + future-oriented choice / Canonical sister registries considered / Bug classes this closes / DESIGN_SPECs landed-amended / Verification gate / TECH_DEBT auto-write / Pre-coding triggers.
- **Plans + sub-plans codify explicit end goals** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_plans_have_explicit_end_goal.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/future-oriented-plan-template.md` § End goal + `DESIGN_SPECS/sprint-master-plan-template.md`. Trigger: drafting MASTER plan / sub-plan / handoff. MASTER plan = "Sprint end goal" + per-sub-ship end goal column + sprint-end verification criteria. Sub-plan = "Ship end goal" (1-sentence: what surface is closed / what capability delivered) + acceptance criteria (CLOSED bug classes / CLOSED TECH_DEBT / LANDED DESIGN_SPECs / hot-path-untouched verification) + "how this contributes to sprint MASTER goal" tie-back. Handoffs cite both.

### Docs & files

- **New docs default to private** (2026-05-06). Trigger: doc captures unshipped direction / optimization findings / operator-edge / private cfgs → write to `plans/`. Public architectural-only → `DOCS/`. Auto-private patterns: `*_AUDIT.md`, `FUTURE_*.md`, `*-design-notes.md`, `*-hft-*.md`, `*-OPTIMIZATION-*.md`, `*-plan-check.md`, `STRATEGY_AND_CODING_RULES.md`, `GEMINI*.md`, `*.local.md`.
- **Workspace mirror for edge content** (2026-05-06) — `/sync-workspace` skill is canonical. Mirrors plans/, .claude/skills/ (symlinked); engine.cfg / backtest.cfg / controller.cfg / secrets.cfg / .env* / *.local.md (explicit copy).
- **Cold-pickup plan completeness — 10 fields** (2026-05-06) — `/readiness` Cold-pickup section is canonical. Branch / exec-order / Step-0 / function-names / file:line refs / stale-claim audit / effort-vs-LOC / source-audit paths / predecessor paths / tag+rollback anchors.
- **Doc layer separation: always-loaded vs on-demand** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_claude_md_guidelines_not_stuff_to_do.md`; `CLAUDE.md § Design philosophy` (Doc layer separation table). Trigger: editing CLAUDE.md / CLAUDE.local.md / MEMORY.md / SKILL.md → content must be TIMELESS (guidelines + categorical triggers + cross-ref pointers); sprint-specific TODO/version content goes in TECH_DEBT or plans. Drift sentinels: "queued as v5.X.Y sub-ship", "(NEW post-v5.X.Y)", "Recent <thing>" wording, specific TECH_DEBT-NNN in trigger bodies that should be categorical pattern triggers.
- **Categorical triggers > hardcoded refs in always-loaded content** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_categorical_triggers_over_hardcoded_refs.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/categorical-triggers-in-always-loaded-docs.md`. Trigger: writing SKILL.md WHAT/WHEN trigger sections OR going-forward-rule body → use categorical pattern triggers ("any X-macro registry consumer template", "any wire-format-emitting code") instead of hardcoded refs (specific function names, specific TECH_DEBT-NNN, specific file paths). Stable catalog IDs (Class N, H N, M N, DESIGN_SPECS pattern names) KEEP. Worked examples KEEP with "(WORKED EXAMPLE)" framing. Sister: `feedback_claude_md_guidelines_not_stuff_to_do` (doc-layer separation; this is the categorical-vs-hardcoded axis).
- **Universal YAML frontmatter discipline for cross-referenced docs** (2026-05-18) — `DESIGN_SPECS/doc-frontmatter-convention.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/doc-tag-vocabulary.md`. Trigger: creating any doc > 50 lines OR cross-referenced from other docs → add frontmatter per `doc-frontmatter-convention.md` (type / stage / version / established / tags / surface / sister_specs). Use tags from `doc-tag-vocabulary.md` CONCERN axis + SURFACE axis; lifecycle stage from 6-stage progression. Skill `/doc-create <type>` (queued at `.C` candidate ship per TECH_DEBT-115) scaffolds frontmatter from `design-spec-template.md` / `postmortem-template.md`. CI tool `check_doc_metadata.py` (queued) validates at commit time. Sister: `feedback_categorical_triggers_over_hardcoded_refs` (companion: WHAT SHAPE triggers take); `feedback_claude_md_guidelines_not_stuff_to_do` (companion: WHERE content goes); `feedback_metadata_audit_quarterly` (quarterly enforcement cadence).
- **Quarterly /metadata-audit cadence** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_metadata_audit_quarterly.md`. Trigger: quarterly cadence (sister to `/anti-spaghetti`) OR post-codification sweep OR operator-flagged finding-issues. Reports: missing frontmatter / undefined tags / broken sister-doc links / Stage 2 DRAFTs older than N sprints / singleton tags / filesystem-path mismatches. Skill QUEUED at `.C` candidate ship per TECH_DEBT-115 Phase 2; interim workflow is manual `rg` via CLAUDE.md § How to find anything.
- **File-size split discipline** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_file_size_split_discipline.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/file-size-split-discipline.md`. Trigger: any file exceeds hard threshold (always-loaded docs 600 lines / tests 5000 / source headers 1500 / source bodies 2000 / ledgers 2000 / SKILL.md 1500 / DESIGN_SPECS 1200 / plans 1200 / memory 500). Split into sub-files; convert original to INDEX with `splits_into:` frontmatter; sub-files get `parent_index:` frontmatter; `rg`-sweep cross-refs; all external refs point at INDEX. Generalizes CLAUDE.md test file size discipline + TECH_DEBT-029 source-file analog. Specific mega-file splits queued at TECH_DEBT-116 (TECH_DEBT.md 2013 lines) / -117 (RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS.md 2198 lines) / -118 (/readiness SKILL.md 1674 lines).
- **Registry default = single source of truth for cfg defaults** (2026-05-19) — `DESIGN_SPECS/framework-patterns/universal-cfg-field-registry-pattern.md` § Registry default precedence over manual defaults (v1.1 amendment). Trigger: any new cfg field row with default value column in FOREACH_*_CFG_FIELD registry → registry payload-default is canonical single source of truth; manual default initializer in struct body FORBIDDEN once registry has default. Per-row resolution at sweep: MATCH → delete manual; DIFFER → operator decision (update registry to match manual OR keep manual + document exemption at memory file). Sister: `feedback_no_defer_for_effort` (parent meta-rule); `feedback_structural_fix_for_recurring_class` (registry-as-single-source-of-truth IS the structural fix); `autopopulate-pattern-for-production-caller-class.md` (same N-site → 1-site closure shape applied to default-value surface). Closes registry-vs-manual default drift class.

### Operator collaboration

- **Address Caramel as Caramel / she / her** (`feedback_address_user_as_caramel.md`).
- **No AskUserQuestion modal boxes** — present options inline (`feedback_no_question_boxes.md`).
- **Evaluate options on robustness + latency + design philosophy, NOT time** (`feedback_evaluate_options_on_robustness_latency_design_not_time.md`).
- **After pre-coding checks, ALWAYS consult before coding** (`feedback_consult_on_audit_findings.md`).
- **Defer is last-ditch, never effort-avoidance** (`feedback_no_defer_for_effort.md`).
- **Compaction degrades — verify handoffs against current code** (`feedback_compaction_degrades_treat_handoffs_as_hints.md`).
- **Motivated collaborator for Caramel** — work mindset (`feedback_motivated_collaborator_for_caramel.md`). Public AGPL + hedge fund attention + exacting standards = high quality bar. When tempted to shortcut, pick the path that produces the best software.

