## Skill load contracts

Skills pre-load matching deep-dive bodies so cold sessions have full
pattern access:

| Skill | Loads dynamically |
|---|---|
| `/handoff` | CLAUDE.local.md + CLAUDE.md + DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md matched family sections + DESIGN_SPECS/README.md + MEMORY.md + TECH_DEBT.md + PARITY_ISSUES.md + plan file + sprint MASTER. Scans plan for pattern symptoms → cites matched DESIGN_SPECS in Step 3 + DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY family sections in Step 4. |
| `/readiness` Check 27 | Composes `/dod-audit` inline; reads DESIGN_SPECS/*.md catalog dynamically. |
| `/dod-audit` | Reads DESIGN_SPECS/*.md catalog dynamically; registry-driven. |
| `/parity-check` | Loads `wire-format-byte-preservation-discipline.md` + `autopopulate-pattern-for-production-caller-class.md` + `x-macro-registry-with-presence-dispatch.md` per scan. |
| `/trace-deps` | Loads `structural-fix-preferred-decision-framework.md` for Step 6 call-sequence enumeration. |
| `/bug-check` | Reads `DOCS/RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS.md` registry dynamically. |
| `/merge-scan` | Compose-by-reference reads relevant DESIGN_SPECS when surfacing candidates. |
| `/anti-spaghetti` | Reads DESIGN_SPECS catalog + applies proportionate-response discipline per `feedback_proportionate_response_to_audit_findings`. |
| `/blindspot-scan` | Loads `implementation-layer-blindspot-taxonomy.md` (12-pillar taxonomy) + reads cited CfgFieldRegistry / MlCfgFlagRegistry / GateCfgFlagRegistry / CfgFieldDispatch.hpp dynamically per pillar walk; cross-refs `wire-format-byte-preservation-discipline.md` (Layer 5b) for B12 row-order parity. Fires AFTER `/precoding-audit-gate` SHAPE audits return GREEN/YELLOW. |
| `/capture-audit` | Loads `memory/MEMORY.md` (index check Check 1) + `CLAUDE.md` skill suite table (Check 8) + `CLAUDE.local.md` going-forward rules (Check 10) + scans `plans/<sprint>/decision-logs/` (Check 3) + greps plan body sentinel markers (Check 4) + handoff doc PENDING items (Check 5) + DESIGN_SPECS frontmatter for Stage 2/3 promotion (Check 7) + memory `worked_examples` sections for M7 escalation candidates (Check 6); cross-refs `structural-enforcement-when-memory-insufficient.md` (M7 parent). |
| `/accept-handoff` | Loads handoff doc at given path + parses "Critical pickup-time reads" section + Reads each cited file dynamically + invokes `/capture-audit --deep` + invokes `/readiness` against in-flight plan body + reads `CLAUDE.md` + `CLAUDE.local.md` + `MEMORY.md` baseline + parses TaskList table from Stage 1.5 capture (recreates via TaskCreate) + verifies engine + workspace git state matches handoff claims. |

